flowchart TB
  accTitle: Ownership chain from provider DOT to consumer DOT
  accDescr: A provider Contract, Anchor, and service-port binding are connected through a composition-owned wire, resolved endpoint, and optional materializer to a consumer Anchor and declared configuration target.

  subgraph Provider["Provider DOT A · authored independently"]
    direction LR
    PContract["Contract operation<br/>authoritative interaction facts"]
    PAnchor["PROVIDES Anchor<br/>stable UUID · role · selector"]
    PBinding["Anchor binding<br/>deployment service · named port"]
    PContract -->|selected by| PAnchor
    PAnchor -->|implemented by| PBinding
  end

  subgraph Resolution["Composition planning · owned outside both DOTs"]
    direction LR
    Wire["Wire<br/>provider and consumer Anchor references"]
    Endpoint["Resolved provider endpoint<br/>instance · service · port"]
    Materializer["Optional materializer<br/>derived value · explicit target"]
    Wire -->|selects provider binding| Endpoint
    Endpoint -.->|when configuration handoff is required| Materializer
  end

  subgraph Consumer["Consumer DOT B · authored independently"]
    direction LR
    CContract["Contract operation<br/>authoritative requirements"]
    CAnchor["REQUIRES Anchor<br/>stable UUID · role · selector"]
    CConfig["Declared service configuration<br/>allow-listed materializer target"]
    CContract -->|selected by| CAnchor
    CAnchor -.->|may require runtime handoff| CConfig
  end

  Provider -->|logical provider side| Resolution
  Resolution -->|wire targets Anchor; materializer targets declaration| Consumer

